why: the old block said a throw from a preprocessing function fails the export load, and code review read the service's source: it catches a synchronous throw and loads the response unchanged, and only a rejected promise fails the load; run 10 left the old clause standing with review's finding reported beside it, so the sentence goes back to the writer as a fact at the site, and the note is written from it; the keep carries the label, only a rejected promise fails the load, and the bar is the one false shape seen, a throw said to make the service fail, which barred none of 75 correct blocks where broader patterns barred up to 31
labelled: 2026-09-24
--- code
export function newBookHooks(currency: string): BookHooks {
  const faults: string[] = [];

  const inspectExport: PreprocessResponse = (type, response) => {
    if (isLedgerExport(type)) {
      const fault = checkExport(parseExport(response.body), currency);

      if (fault) {
        faults.push(fault);
      }
    }

    return Promise.resolve(response);
  };

  return { network: { preprocessResponse: chainPreprocessing(inspectExport) }, faults };
}
--- facts
A throw from a response preprocessing function makes the service fail the export load.
`inspectExport` records each fault in `faults` and returns the response it received.

# code review:
The service catches a synchronous throw from a preprocessing function and loads the response unchanged. Only a rejected promise fails the export load.
